# The firmware the Linux driver processes load, from linux-firmware
# (https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git).
#
# `scripts/linuxfw.py fetch` fetches each file named here at the release
# named here into build/firmware/<path>, and refuses any whose bytes are not
# the hash given. The files are not committed: each is a binary under its
# own licence, which linux-firmware's WHENCE names. `scripts/pikvm.py stage`
# puts them on the boot medium as modules `firmware/<path>`, which the kernel
# places under /lib/firmware (design-decisions 1592).
#
# Moving the release is one commit: the tag, and every file's hash, taken
# from a fetch over HTTPS from kernel.org; once committed, these lines are
# the trust anchor.
release 20261019

# mt7925e, the test PC's MediaTek RZ717 (PCI 14C3:0717): its MCU's ROM
# patch and its WM firmware (mt792x.h, MT7925_ROM_PATCH and
# MT7925_FIRMWARE_WM). WHENCE: "Licence: Redistributable. See
# LICENCE.mediatek for details."
